- Story & Context: Holed up in an abandoned telegraph outpost overlooking the grinding moraines of Sermeq Kujalleq, operator Einar Blom discovered a forgotten pouch of postal telegrams from 1988 that had arrived decades after the coastal recipient had vanished. Tortured by the dead words, Einar routed his tape-saturated synthesizer loops and crying blues guitar leads through the glacier's drainage flues, watching the meltwater slurry warp his delayed notes into sorrowful, whistling microtones. The air hung thick with the reek of ozone and rotting kelp as his pitch-dropped voice lamented over a sluggish deep house thrum: "The postmark faded before your handwriting dried." His tape recorder caught the glacier groaning in precise harmony, swallowing his confession under fifty tons of collapsing slush.
